      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents argue that school vouchers provide parents with choices, allowing them to send their children to private schools that might better fit their needs. They believe this encourages competition among schools, ultimately improving the quality of public education for everyone. Conversely, opponents argue that vouchers drain essential funding from public schools, potentially weakening the entire public education system. Furthermore, critics often point out that vouchers can exacerbate educational inequality.",
      "source": "target",
